    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentJavaTitle">The server needs Java {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentJavaAction">Download Java and start</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaTitle">The Minecraft licence agreement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaLine">A Minecraft server only starts once Mojang's agreement (EULA) is accepted</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaDetail">By pressing the button you confirm that you have read it and accept it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_ConsentEulaAction">I accept, start</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WaysTitle">How friends connect</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WaysHint">Switch on one way or several. The invite carries what is on and already working.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayOff">Off</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayPending">Comes on when the server is running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayRelay">Friends only</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayRelayText">Friends with STlauncher join by the invite. Nothing to set up: the connection goes through a relay server, no ports to open.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayNotConfigured">The relay server is not set up yet, so this way is not available. The other two work without it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayWorking">Connecting to the relay {0}…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayReady">Ready: friends join by the invite</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayUnreachable">The relay {0} does not answer. The launcher keeps trying.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayBusy">The relay is at its limit right now. The launcher keeps trying.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RelayRejected">The relay refused the connection: the launcher may need an update.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirect">Directly</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirectWarning">Open ports are required. This works only when your provider gives you a public IP address and the router has UPnP on, or port {0} is forwarded by hand. Otherwise friends will not get through: use the invite way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_WayDirectText">Friends connect straight to your computer. The launcher asks the router to open port {0} and checks from outside that the server can be reached. The port closes together with the server.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectWorking">Talking to the router and checking from outside…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectReady">Ready, checked from outside</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectReadyUnverified">The port is open. There is nothing to check it from outside with: no relay is set up</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectNoGateway">The router did not answer: UPnP is switched off in it, or it has none. Switch UPnP on in the router's settings, or pick another way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectRefused">The router refused to open the port.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectBehindNat">Your provider keeps the router behind a shared address, so a direct connection cannot work: use the invite way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectNotReachable">The router opened the port, yet the server cannot be reached from outside: the provider or the Windows firewall is in the way.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_DirectError">The router stopped answering. Switch the way off and on again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteNeedsServer">Start the server first: the invite is put together while it runs.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteNeedsWay">Switch on at least one way of connecting and wait until it is ready.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteBusy">Putting the invite together…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedShort">The invite is copied: {0}. Send it to a friend: they copy it and press “A friend's build” on the home screen. It works while your server is running. Remember to put their nickname on the list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortNoRelay">This is a short invite, and the launcher does not know the server that keeps such invites yet. Ask the friend for the long one, or try again later.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortFetching">Asking for the invite {0}…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortUnreachable">The server that keeps invites does not answer. Check the connection and try again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ShortOffline">Nobody answers to the invite {0}: the friend's server is not running right now, or the code has a typo.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopied">The invite is copied. Send it to a friend: they press “A friend's build” on the home screen. Remember to put their nickname on the list.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedMissing">The invite is copied. These mods are not on Modrinth and have to be handed over separately: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteCopiedNoBuild">The invite is copied without the build: Modrinth did not answer. The friend will need a build of their own for {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_InviteFailed">The invite could not be put together: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Removed">The server “{0}” is off the list. Its folder with the world is intact: {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_RemoveFailed">Could not take the server off the list: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_SaveFailed">Could not save the server's settings: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_LoadFailed">Could not read the list of servers: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_Unreadable">A server could not be read and was left untouched: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTitle">The server is still running</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseText">The server “{0}” is running. Closing the launcher stops it: the world is saved, the players are disconnected and the addresses opened for friends are closed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirm">Stop and close</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirmUpdate">Stop and update</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTunnelTitle">You are on a friend's server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseTextTunnel">The game is connected to the friend's server through the launcher. Closing the launcher breaks that connection.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseConfirmTunnel">Close anyway</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Host_CloseCancel">Keep it open</x:String>

    <!-- My server: friends' servers and invites -->
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Title">Friends' servers</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Paste">paste an invite</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Empty">Servers you have been invited to show up here. Copy a friend's invite - the line that starts with STS1. - and press “paste an invite”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ClipboardEmpty">The clipboard holds neither a build code nor an invite. Copy the invite (ST-XXXXX-XXXXX) or the line that starts with STB1. or STS1. and try again.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_DefaultName">A friend's server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Subtitle">{0} · Minecraft {1} · {2}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_SubtitleNoHost">Minecraft {0} · {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Build">Build “{0}”</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_BuildGone">The build for this server was deleted. Paste the invite again to bring it back.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Play">Play</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Remove">Take the server off the list</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Removed">The server “{0}” is off the list. Its build stays on the Builds tab.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_SaveFailed">Could not save the list of friends' servers: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteTitle">An invite from {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteTitleNoHost">An invite to a server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteServer">The server “{0}”</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteKnown">You already have this server</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteKnownDetail">Only the addresses to connect by are updated. The build “{0}” stays as it is.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildAdd">The build “{0}” is added</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildDetail">Files: {0}, {1}. Downloaded from {2}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildMissing">Not in the invite, your friend hands them over: {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildEmpty">A build without mods is made</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteBuildNoFiles">Minecraft {0} · {1}, no mods. The game's files are downloaded on the first start.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteWays">How the game connects</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_WayDirect">directly, {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_WayRelay">through the relay {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_WayPublic">by the public address {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteNothingStarts">Nothing starts now</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteNothingStartsDetail">The server appears in the list below. The game starts when you press “Play”.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteAccept">Add</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_InviteDecline">Do not add</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Added">The server “{0}” is added. Press “Play” once your friend has started it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Updated">The addresses of the server “{0}” are updated</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_AddFailed">The server could not be added: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_GameBusy">The game is already running or starting</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Connecting">Looking for the server…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ConnectedDirect">Connected directly. If the game does not join by itself, the server's address is {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ConnectedRelay">Connected through the relay. If the game does not join by itself, the server's address is {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_ConnectedPublic">Connected by the public address. If the game does not join by itself, the server's address is {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_Offline">The server does not answer. Ask your friend to start it and press “Play” again. If their address has changed, ask for a new invite.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_OfflineRelayDown">The relay does not answer and there is no other way to the server. Try again later.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_OfflineRelayBusy">The relay is at its limit right now. Try again in a minute.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_OfflineHost">Your friend's launcher is not there, or their server is off. Ask them to start the server.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Friends_PlayFailed">Could not connect: {0}</x:String>

    <!-- Skins: the library, the editor, publishing -->
    <x:String x:Key="Nav_Skins">Skins</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Title">Skins</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Subtitle">Your skin library: keep skins, draw them, and put them on your figure in the launcher. Other players see a skin only through the skin system their server uses - that is what publishing is for.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_New">New skin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewFrom">START FROM</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewSteve">Steve</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewSteveHint">classic model, arms 4 pixels wide</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewAlex">Alex</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewAlexHint">slim arms, 3 pixels wide</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NewName">New skin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_AddPng">Add PNG</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_AddPngHint">Choose skin files on this computer. The files are copied into the library; the originals stay where they are.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PickTitle">Choose skin files</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PickType">Minecraft skin (PNG)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ByNick">By nickname</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ByNickTitle">ANOTHER PLAYER'S SKIN</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ByNickHint">Type a nickname: the launcher finds the skin that player wears (a licensed account, TLauncher or Ely.by) and adds it to the library.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ByNickWatermark">Player's nickname</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ByNickAdd">Find and add</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NickNotFound">No skin was found for «{0}»: there is no such player, or they wear the default one.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_NickAdded">The skin of «{0}» is now in the library.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomTitle">Random skins</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomText">Skins other people uploaded recently: look, save one you like and make it your own. The feed is public and nobody curates it; the skins have no names. Taken from mineskin.org when you press the button.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomShow">Show</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomMore">Show others</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomLoading">Loading skins…</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomNone">The feed did not answer, or had nothing that is a whole skin. Try again in a minute.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomPreviewHint">Look at it on the model</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomPreviewTitle">A random skin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomPreviewText">Drag the figure with the mouse to turn it and look from every side.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomSaveToLibrary">Save to the library</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomSave">Save</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomSavedMark">In the library</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomName">Random {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RandomSaved">Saved to the library as «{0}». It can be renamed and edited there.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveCurrent">Save the current skin</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveCurrentHint">Copy the skin your figure wears now into the library: the one found by your nickname at Mojang, TLauncher or ely.by.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SavedCurrent">The skin from your figure is now in the library as "{0}".</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveCurrentFailed">This skin could not be read, so it was not saved.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DefaultName">Steve</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_WornTag">Worn</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_WornPill">Worn in the launcher</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_EmptyTitle">The library is empty so far</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_EmptyText">Draw a new skin, add a PNG from this computer, or save the skin your figure wears now. Files of 64×64 fit, and so do the old 64×32 ones - the launcher converts those to the new layout.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DropHint">A skin PNG can be dropped straight onto this page.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DropHere">Drop to add to the library</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DropHereHint">PNG files of 64×64 and 64×32 fit</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_AddedCount">Skins added: {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ConvertedCount">Converted from the old 64×32 format: {0}.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RefusedNotPng">"{0}" is not a PNG picture. A Minecraft skin is a PNG file.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RefusedSize">"{0}" is {1}×{2}. A Minecraft skin is a PNG of 64×64, or 64×32 in the old format.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RefusedUnreadable">"{0}" could not be read: the file is damaged or saved in an unusual PNG format.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RefusedError">"{0}": {1}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ModelClassic">Classic model</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ModelSlim">Slim arms</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_AddedOn">added {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Rename">Rename</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_RenameHint">Skin name</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Wear">Wear</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_WornNotice">"{0}" is now on your figure in the launcher. Other players will see this skin once it is published to the skin system their server uses.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_TakeOff">Take off</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_TakeOffHint">The figure will show the skin found by your nickname again. The skin stays in the library.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_TakenOff">The figure shows the skin found by your nickname again. The skin stays in the library.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Edit">Edit</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Duplicate">Duplicate</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_CopyName">{0} - copy</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Delete">Delete</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DeleteAsk">Delete this skin from the library? Its file will be removed from the disk.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_DeleteConfirm">Delete</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Deleted">"{0}" was deleted from the library.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_HonestNote">"Wear" changes the figure in the launcher only. In the game other players see a skin once it is published to the skin system their server uses.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SourceOwn">Own</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_OpenFromHome">Skin library and editor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_FromLibrary">Skin from your library: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LibraryNoneWorn">No library skin is worn yet. Open Skins and press Wear on one.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishButton">Put it on in the game</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishMicrosoft">Microsoft account (licensed)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishMsHint">The file is ready and its path is in the clipboard. On the minecraft.net page that opened, sign in with your Microsoft account, press 'Upload skin' and choose the file (paste the path with Ctrl+V in the file dialog).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishIntro">A skin is put on at the site of the service other players see you through. The launcher saves the PNG to the skins/publish folder, copies the path to the file, shows it in Explorer and opens the right page.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishElyHint">The file is ready and its path is in the clipboard. On the ely.by page that opened, sign in, choose the file (paste the path with Ctrl+V in the file dialog), upload it and put the skin on your account.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishTlHint">The file is ready and its path is in the clipboard. On the TLauncher page that opened, sign in, press "Upload skin" and choose the file (paste the path with Ctrl+V in the file dialog).</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PublishFailed">The file could not be prepared: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_OpenFailed">"{0}" could not be opened: the file is damaged or is not a skin.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_BackToLibrary">Back to the library</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_EditorLabel">SKIN EDITOR</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_StateSaved">Everything is saved</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_StateUnsaved">There are unsaved changes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Undo">Undo (Ctrl+Z)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Redo">Redo (Ctrl+Y)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Save">Save</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveHint">Save to the library (Ctrl+S)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveFailed">The skin could not be saved: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_SaveGone">This skin is no longer in the library, so there is nowhere to save it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LibraryUnreadable">The list of your skins could not be read right now: another program may be holding the file. The skins themselves are safe. Open this page again in a moment.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Tool">TOOL</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolPencil">Pencil</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolEraser">Eraser</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolEraserHint">Erases to transparent. On the base layer the game shows transparent spots as black.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolFill">Fill</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolFillHint">Paints the touching pixels of the same colour, within one face.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolPicker">Pipette</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ToolPickerHint">Takes a colour from the drawing. The right mouse button does the same with any tool.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Colour">COLOUR</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_HexHint">The colour as #RRGGBB</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Recent">RECENT COLOURS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Mirror">Mirror</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_MirrorHint">Draw on both halves at once: right arm and left, right leg and left, the two sides of the head and the body.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Grid">Grid</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LayerBase">Base</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LayerOverlay">Overlay</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LayerBaseHint">The skin itself: skin and clothes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_LayerOverlayHint">The second layer over the base: hat, jacket, sleeves, trousers. The base shows faintly.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_KeysHint">Ctrl+Z undo · Ctrl+Y redo · right button is the pipette</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Preview">HOW IT LOOKS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_PreviewHint">Drag the figure to turn it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_Model">MODEL</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ModelClassicShort">Classic</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ModelSlimShort">Slim arms</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_ModelHint">Classic has arms 4 pixels wide, like Steve. Slim has 3, like Alex.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_UnsavedTitle">Save the changes?</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_UnsavedText">The skin has unsaved changes. Leaving without saving loses them.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_UnsavedStay">Back to the drawing</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_UnsavedDiscard">Do not save</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Skins_UnsavedSave">Save and leave</x:String>
